  "narrative": {
    "intro": "General Dynamics Land Systems has $1.3B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. General Dynamics Land Systems won 310 obligations so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $4.1M. Obligations fell 16.3% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows variability: FY21 recorded $2.5B, FY22 recorded $4B, FY23 recorded $3.5B, FY24 recorded $2.6B, FY25 recorded $1.5B, and FY26 recorded $1.3B. Military armored vehicle work dominates the current-year portfolio with $1.2B assigned to Military Armored Vehicle, Tank, and Tank Component Manufacturing. Other FY2026 markets include General Automotive Repair at $69.7M and a mix of engineering, electronics, and support services in smaller amounts, such as Facilities Support Services at $9.9M and Bare Printed Circuit Board Manufacturing at $7.9M. The FY2026 totals are partial, reflecting fiscal year to date activity rather than a full-year result. This snapshot shows a heavy concentration in armored vehicle manufacturing alongside a long tail of maintenance, electronics, and services awards.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are General Dynamics Land Systems' FY2026 federal obligations?",
        "body": "General Dynamics Land Systems concentrated most of FY2026 obligations in military armored vehicles, with $1.2B in Military Armored Vehicle, Tank, and Tank Component Manufacturing. General Dynamics Land Systems recorded $69.7M in General Automotive Repair and much smaller totals across nine other NAICS markets. General Dynamics Land Systems has 310 awards this fiscal year, producing an average award size of $4.1M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "How has General Dynamics Land Systems' federal revenue changed over recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "General Dynamics Land Systems' obligations trended higher in FY22 and FY23 before declining: FY21 was $2.5B, FY22 was $4B, FY23 was $3.5B, FY24 was $2.6B, FY25 was $1.5B, and FY26 is $1.3B. General Dynamics Land Systems' obligations fell 16.3% year over year in the current fiscal period."
      }
    ]
  },
